    "description": "Source: 2026-08-04 weekly sync. Lina \\[06:10\\]: 'a potential field on the signup record to say like payment sent, like a button... to cross off that like the signup record has been paid in Salesforce.' Kobi \\[09:05\\]: 'we'll add it to the ops view for sign-up records for a payment sent, and we'll table the bigger conversation around actual payout code generation for later.'\n\nAdd a Payment Sent checkbox to the Sign Up Ops view. This is the ONLY payout artefact kept in Phase 1 — payout code generation is deferred (see DECISION-05 / BUILD-05).\n\nContext: today Wagertech runs one sheet for bank transfers per sign-up and another for referral payments. This closes the loop for the testing rep.\n\nFollow-ups noted, NOT in this card:\n\n* A SEPARATE checkbox will be needed for redeposit payments (Lina: 'redeposits are kind of a different thing when it comes to payouts').\n\n* Emily raised importing already-paid sign-ups at launch so the dataset is not gapped — no decision taken, tracked separately.\n\n",
